- phrase each step as a concrete action naming an example of what the reader creates (e.g. 'add a new <Base> named Foo<Base>');
- list every required API with its full signature, including parameters, grouped by category;
- for an extension guide that mixes these, split it into a basic section with only the steps the reader must perform (optionally followed by a verification step), leaving out internals that work automatically, and a separate advanced/performance section that states, for each optional feature, its default behavior and exactly which setting or field to set, or what to implement, to opt in.
